# Clockspeed - .rgignore
#
# Ripgrep already honours .gitignore, so everything generated, local or
# publisher-owned is out of a search by default. This file covers the one case
# .gitignore cannot: paths that ARE tracked and MUST stay tracked, but which are
# historical rather than current.
#
# CONVENTIONS.md section 2: "Dated artifacts go to docs/_archive/, excluded from
# ripgrep searches via .rgignore or an explicit glob, so they never pollute a
# search for current truth."
#
# The failure this prevents: a grep for a rule, a path or a decision returns a
# hit from a superseded session note, that hit is read as current, and work is
# redone or a refuted idea is re-pitched. Rediscovery is the dominant failure
# mode (CONVENTIONS.md section 0, corollary 3), and a stale grep hit is how it
# gets in.
#
# To search the archive deliberately, pass --no-ignore-vcs --no-ignore or point
# ripgrep straight at docs/_archive/. Being excluded here is not being hidden;
# it is not being returned by accident.

docs/_archive/
